\begin{theorem}
There is an orientation-preserving smooth diffeomorphism \(d:S^6\to X\), with \(d\simeq g\) and \(d^{-1}\simeq h_X\) for the original maps of Section 9.
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
The original stable tangent frame in \eqref{courseIII:integral-homology-and-sphere-recognition:eq:10.6} enters the full Pontryagin–Thom comparison and geometric framing proof cited above. For the whole six-dimensional framed bordism group, the \cref{courseIII:sphere-twists-and-the-original-smooth-six-sphere-comparison:twist-general-stable-framing} proves the complete tangent-to-normal framing homotopy without assuming a complex structure; this is an independent bundle calculation before the sphere argument. The latter's Sections 8–9 prove framed bordism invariance and identify the original sixth framed bordism group with \(\mathbb F_2\) through its quadratic invariant. The original \(H_3(X;\mathbb F_2)=0\) makes that invariant zero; injectivity therefore yields an actual framed nullbordism \(W\) with its specified boundary identification \(\iota_X:X\to\partial W\).
